		Therefore, $P_{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y})$ and $P'_{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y}|{\hat{\mathbf{x}}})$ having the same factorization and the corresponding conditional distributions being equal implies that $P_{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y}) = P'_{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y}|{\hat{\mathbf{x}}})$.


